From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-controller 9992: do not dereference a radio that was never filled

cntlr_send_ap_mld_configuration_request() and its bSTA twin walk n->radiolist
and read r->radio_el->wifi7caps_* without checking r->radio_el. A node whose
radios were never populated carries netif_radio entries with radio_el == NULL,
and the read is a NULL dereference.

Such nodes exist by construction, from two sources measured on hardware
2026-07-20:

  - db_restore() hydrates the model from mapc.db at t=0, before any agent has
    reported radios;
  - a boot-time double-create (nodelist loop plus restore) leaves an orphan
    node object with radios=0.

The crash path is not exotic - it is the ordinary one. cntlr_check_config_diff()
walks the entire agentlist on any config change (onboarding, a link flap, a node
arriving), so a phantom is reached as readily as a real node:

	EXIT=139 (128+11, SIGSEGV), reproduced 2/2 outside procd
	core pc=0x423a74, x0=0
	addr2line -> cntlr_check_config_diff, cntlr.c
	             -> cntlr_send_ap_mld_configuration_request

It was invisible for weeks because procd respawn logs nothing, OpenWrt does not
write userspace segfaults to dmesg, and procd does not pass ulimit -c to its
children, so no core was produced until one was forced.

The guard was written on 2026-07-20 and landed in the node-identity series in
the easymesh-r6 tree; it was never carried into this patch series. Verified
absent in map-controller 6.5.0.18.

This is a prerequisite for 9993 (node expiry margin). Raising NODE_EXPIRE_TIME
from 65 s to 180 s triples how long a phantom survives, and the crash needs a
config change to land inside that window - so widening the window without this
guard would trade one reliability problem for a worse one.

continue rather than bail: a node may legitimately hold one filled radio and
one not yet reported, and skipping only the empty entry keeps the Wi-Fi 7 scan
correct. r is used after the loop, but only when has_wifi7 is true, which
implies the loop stopped on an entry that passed the guard.

Not fixed here: the same class of unguarded r->radio_el reads exists elsewhere
in cntlr_map.c (beacon metrics request, channel scan request). Those sit on
different call paths and are left for a separate change rather than widened
into this one.

--- a/src/cntlr_map.c
+++ b/src/cntlr_map.c
@@ -4747,6 +4747,15 @@
 		return -1;
 
 	list_for_each_entry(r, &n->radiolist, list) {
+		/* A node restored from mapc.db, or one duplicated by a
+		 * boot-time double-create, carries netif_radio entries whose
+		 * radio_el was never filled - radios=0 on the wire. Config
+		 * diff walks the whole agentlist, so such a node reaches this
+		 * loop and dereferences NULL (SIGSEGV, procd respawn, forever).
+		 */
+		if (!r->radio_el)
+			continue;
+
 		if (cntlr_radio_support_wifi7(&r->radio_el->wifi7caps_ap)) {
 			has_wifi7 = true;
 			break;
@@ -4776,6 +4785,15 @@
 		return -1;
 
 	list_for_each_entry(r, &n->radiolist, list) {
+		/* A node restored from mapc.db, or one duplicated by a
+		 * boot-time double-create, carries netif_radio entries whose
+		 * radio_el was never filled - radios=0 on the wire. Config
+		 * diff walks the whole agentlist, so such a node reaches this
+		 * loop and dereferences NULL (SIGSEGV, procd respawn, forever).
+		 */
+		if (!r->radio_el)
+			continue;
+
 		if (cntlr_radio_support_wifi7(&r->radio_el->wifi7caps_bsta)) {
 			has_wifi7 = true;
 			break;
